# Live scenario tests use credentials from your authenticated Azure development tools.
# These tests create/delete testsmrg-js-* resource groups and temporary containers/RBAC
# assignments, approve test private endpoints, and run transfers using shared infrastructure.
# Confirm access and ownership before running with TEST_MODE=live or TEST_MODE=record.
#
# SUBSCRIPTION_ID=<subscription for temporary test resource groups>
# STORAGE_MOVER_TEST_LOCATION=<supported Storage Mover region>
# STORAGE_MOVER_PRIVATE_LINK_SERVICE_RESOURCE_GROUP=<approved PLS resource group>
# STORAGE_MOVER_PRIVATE_LINK_SERVICE_NAME=<approved PLS name>
#
# The PLS must be in the XDataMove-Synthetics subscription used by testHelper.ts.
# The private-bucket scenario also requires connectivity to the configured private S3 source.
# By default, ordinary scenarios run in eastus and C2C/Connection scenarios in westcentralus,
# using E2E-Management-RGsyn/test-pls-wcs. A location override applies to both groups.
# Infrastructure overrides apply in live/record mode only; playback retains recorded settings.
# Live mode does not update recordings or change assets.json.
# To record the existing scenarios, set TEST_MODE=record and leave STORAGE_MOVER_TEST_LOCATION
# unset so ordinary/C2C scenarios retain their respective playback regions. PLS name/resource
# group overrides are sanitized to the playback defaults. Run TEST_MODE=playback without live
# credentials afterward. Publishing recordings and updating assets.json is a separate step.